build: 2026-06-19 v10.34.9 (stability pass — crash-class audio/core fixes)
branch: claude/piano-roll-clip-view-wozlie
includes: A targeted stability pass from a re-verified bug audit. (1) Removed an audio-thread heap allocation in the polyphonic synth mix: each voice's stereo accumulation did a copy-on-write Array copy per block on the render thread; now an in-place vDSP_vadd (audio-thread reviewer PASS) — no malloc on the audio thread. (2) Fixed an out-of-bounds crash path in the lock-free SPSC queue: the overflow "drop-oldest" advanced the head index unmasked, so once it reached capacity the next dequeue indexed one past the buffer; head is now advanced with the same masked compare-and-swap the consumer uses. (3) Fixed a use-after-free in RetroCapture (retroactive loop capture): deinit freed the ring/file pointers without removing the audio tap; it now removes the tap (synchronous) before deallocating. (4) Released a leaked mach port in the real-time thread-priority setup. (5) Decorrelated the polyphonic noise (each voice now seeds its noise PRNG distinctly, so chords don't comb-filter the noise layer). Control-plane + render-path correctness only — no user-facing behaviour change, no change to launch silence or the bio pipeline. Verified: ci.yml (build+test, all platforms) + xcode-compile-check (AUv3 included) green on b30d598. Plus everything from v10.34.3–v10.34.8.
